    "name": "I \u2014 POV first-person scene on street food (transformation reveal)",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "nd_2HNMF9B1BTA667K5D3J715829Y",
        "kind": "prompt",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: POV first-person scene\nTopic: street food\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 12s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_668WWXY0P9QGBJ8W5NTBEQMAG9",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_TC74W847VD7V97Z3JAHPBXR6PG",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_S8R82NT22B8CTB411DS27KP7HH",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.88,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a POV first-person scene about street food for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the POV first-person scene \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a crane-down descending from overhead into a level medium on an 85mm short telephoto, framing with a tight crop that breaks the subject at the frame edge.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with blue-hour ambient with a single warm practical for separation; grade as a Portra-style palette with creamy skin tones and soft greens. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. The response must be a lone prompt paragraph \u2014 strip any header, numbering or sign-off."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_GHB2A9JM0WSYX6YMAYAN0N3G2V",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
        },
        "config": {
          "url": ""
        },
        "name": "Before image"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_5KQWB4V5Y3CDN1845BF7XBZFGH",
        "kind": "concat",
        "position": {
          "x": 350,
          "y": 520
        },
        "config": {
          "separator": "\n\n",
          "appendable_slots": {
